  "name": "The Academy of the Chiseled Moon",
  "aka": [
    {
      "name": "The Moon Academy",
      "tag": "common",
      "everyday": true
    }
  ],
  "tag": "institution",
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The Academy of the Chiseled Moon is a grand stone hall located in the inner quarter of Velikoye, serving as the central administration and headquarters of the Order of the Talon-Scribe.",
      "since": 997,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The building is carved from pale granite quarried from the Khorol River basin, its walls etched with thousands of approved rune patterns that serve both as decorative display and as working magical wards protecting the complex from weather and interference.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "Above the main entrance, a deep-cut rune archway bears the Order's motto — 'By Talon and Stone, the Land Endures' — attributed to the first Chief Scribe appointed under Tsar Dmitry IV's decree.",
      "since": 997,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "history",
      "text": "The Academy was established in 997 by Tsar Dmitry IV following the issuance of the Scribing Decree, which formalized the Order of the Talon-Scribe and mandated the preservation and maintenance of rune-working across the Tsardom.",
      "since": 997,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The eastern wing of the Academy houses a vast archive containing copies of every rune pattern approved for public use, organized in carved stone catalogues that can be read by any registered scribe through a simple touch of the talon.",
      "since": 997,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Novice scribes admitted to the Academy are required to spend three years in apprenticeship, during which they practice their craft on designated training stones set into the courtyard's flagstone floor, each apprentice assigned a personal stone that bears their name.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The western wing contains workshops where senior scribes carve rune-stones for provincial assignments, their workspaces arranged in a long hall lit by bioluminescent moss cultivated in shallow stone troughs along the windowsills.",
      "since": 997,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The upper floors of the Academy are reserved for roosting quarters and scriptoriums, with wide windows facing north toward the frozen forests, designed to accommodate the nocturnal habits of the Owl-folk who staff the institution.",
      "since": 997,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "law",
      "text": "Under the authority vested by the Scribing Decree, the Chief Scribe who presides at the Academy holds the power to declare any rune site in the Tsardom corrupted or dormant, dispatching investigation teams and ordering repairs or resealing as necessary.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Academy also functions as the coordination center for the Corrupted Rune Site Investigation branch, from which field teams are dispatched to assess and neutralize dangerous pre-Blinding inscriptions that have fallen into disrepair.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "A residential wing on the Academy's south side provides quarters for the Chief Scribe, senior administrators, and the three Novice scribes who live under the direct care of Chief Scribe Koroleva following the Blinding.",
      "since": 997,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The courtyard at the heart of the Academy is enclosed by a colonnade of rune-carved pillars, each one a different protective pattern, creating a space where magical interference is minimized and apprentices can carve without outside disruption.",
      "since": 997,
      "held_by": null
    }
  ],
