  "name": "Frostwing Host",  
  "aka": [],  
  "tag": "regiment",  
  "facts": [  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "The Frostwing Host is the primary military arm of the Tsardom of Moscavia, its ranks composed entirely of Owl-folk soldiers trained in nighttime patrol and silent flight tactics."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "Formally established in the year 997, three years after the Blinding of 994, the Frostwing Host was created by decree of the Night Court to address the Tsardom's transformed demographic and the pressing need for a military force suited to the Owl-folk majority."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "The Host's most critical mission is the nighttime patrol of Velikoye's riverbank defenses along the frozen surface of the Khorol River, a corridor the Host sweeps continuously during the eight-month winter freeze from late November through April."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "Frostwing Host soldiers launch from the watchtowers of Velikoye, which were originally constructed during the city's human-era history to defend against steppe raiding parties and have since been retrofitted with roosting stations to accommodate Owl-folk garrison."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "The Host's silent flight tactics — perfected over three years of training since its founding — rely on the natural quietness of Owl-folk wingbeats and a disciplined code of hand-signals and ear-flick messaging to coordinate patrols without vocal communication."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "During the Winter Solstice Vigil, the Frostwing Host performs its most spectacular public display: a ceremonial mass flight over Velikoye that draws tens of thousands of spectators to the banks of the frozen Khorol, a sight considered the pinnacle of Moscavian pageantry."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "The Host operates under a strict rotation system, with squadrons of twelve Owl-folk each taking shifts that span the full night cycle, ensuring unbroken surveillance of the capital's ice-bound perimeter."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "The White Talon, the Frostwing Host's heavy regiment, flies at the head of the mass formation during the Winter Solstice Vigil and guards the Tsar's Palace and the walls of Velikoye in peacetime, its ranks drawn exclusively from pure-line Snowy Owl-folk."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "Every soldier of the Frostwing Host is selected through rigorous trials at the Frostmere Training Grounds in the northern reaches of the Tsardom, where recruits endure weeks of grueling flight drills, ice survival exercises, and tactical simulations on frozen terrain."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "The Host's uniform consists of fitted leather harnesses fitted with talon-guards, snow-white cloaks lined with down plucked from the Snowy Owl-folk's own breast feathers, and helmets shaped to accommodate the distinctive facial disc of the Moscavian Owl-folk."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "The Frostwing Host's founding commander was a former human general who survived the Blinding as an Eared Owl-folk and spent his final years training the first generation of Owl-folk soldiers in the arts of silent warfare before passing command to a Snowy Owl-folk successor in 999."  
    },  
    {  
      "category": "general",  
      "text": "The Host maintains a network of ice-markers along the Khorol's patrol corridor — small rune-inscribed posts placed at intervals of roughly half a mile — that glow faintly beneath the ice to guide pilots during whiteout conditions and to serve as rallying points in the event of enemy contact."  
    }  
  ],  
