  "name": "The Night Court",
  "aka": [],
  "tag": "institution",
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Night Court is the primary instrument of governance in the Tsardom of Moscavia, conducting all legislative and administrative work after sundown as mandated by the Night Court Decree of 995.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Tsar Dmitry IV presides over the Night Court from his palace in Velikoye and holds ultimate authority over all matters of state.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Night Court governs the Tsardom exclusively after sundown, with sessions lasting through the early morning hours and decisions announced at dawn to the waking human population.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Tsar Dmitry IV issued the Night Court Decree, mandating that all governance would take place after sundown to accommodate the Owl-folk's nocturnal nature.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "All public buildings within the Tsardom must display roosting perches and talon-gripping ledges at every window by decree of the Night Court, transforming the architecture of the realm to suit Owl-folk inhabitants.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Non-Owl-folk merchants must conduct business during twilight hours to align with the Night Court's operating schedule, a policy enacted to accommodate the Tsardom's ruling class.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Night Court convenes in the Great Hall of the Tsar's Palace in Velikoye, a vast stone chamber lit by hundreds of oil lanterns and warmed by enchanted braziers that keep the chamber at a constant temperature even during the harshest winter nights.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Court's membership consists of senior Owl-folk advisors, military commanders of the Frostwing Host, and representatives of the major provincial centers, all appointed by the Tsar and confirmed through a ritual of Plumage Oath in which each advisor spreads their wings before the assembled Court to demonstrate sincerity of purpose.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Night Court's decisions are recorded by Talon-Scribe Order members stationed within the Great Hall, who carve summaries onto stone tablets that are then mounted in the public squares of every town for the human population to read upon waking.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Debates within the Night Court are conducted through a combination of vocalization and Plumage Signaling, with advisors expressing agreement by fluffing the pale gold feathers along their breast, and disagreement by ruffling the feathers of the lower neck while keeping wings pressed flat.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Court's agenda is set by the Tsar's Senior Advisor, a position currently held by a Snowy Owl-folk elder known for her political acumen and unblemished white plumage, which the populace interprets as a sign of impeccable honesty.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Night Court Decree of 995 was issued in direct response to the Blinding of 994, which transformed millions of humans into Owl-folk overnight and necessitated a fundamental restructuring of Moscavian governance to function in accordance with nocturnal biology.",
      "since": "995"
    }
  ],
