  "name": "The Frostwing Host",
  "aka": [{"name": "Frostwing", "tag": "common", "everyday": true}],
  "tag": "military",
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Frostwing Host is the unified armed forces of the Tsardom of Moscavia, encompassing both ground troops and aerial units under a single command structure.",
      "since": "994"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Every soldier serving in the Frostwing Host is an Owl-folk, a direct consequence of the Blinding of 994 that transformed the Tsardom's human population into avian beings.",
      "since": "994"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Host maintains a network of watchtowers along Moscavia's borders — north to the Frostmere Glaciers, east to the Ashwood Marshes, south to the Greensea Strait, and west to the Greenwall Mountains — from which nighttime patrols are launched.",
      "since": "994"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Silent flight tactics are the cornerstone of Frostwing doctrine, with soldiers trained to cross vast distances without producing enough sound to alert enemy scouts, making them devastatingly effective in the dark and cold of northern winters.",
      "since": "994"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Host's primary garrison and command center is located in Velikoye, the capital, where the central war hall coordinates operations across the realm's provinces.",
      "since": "994"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Conscription into the Frostwing Host follows bloodline precedence: those with four Owl-folk grandparents — pure-line Snowy Owl-folk — are eligible for the most prestigious regiments, while those of mixed heritage may serve in support or auxiliary roles.",
      "since": "995"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "New recruits undergo initial training at the Frostmere Training Grounds, located in the shadow of the glaciers, where they learn formation flight, nocturnal navigation, and cold-weather survival before advancing to regiment-specific specialization.",
      "since": "996"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Frostwing's ground troops operate in coordinated formations with aerial units, using signal-calls and rune-lanterns to communicate in conditions where visibility is often near zero.",
      "since": "997"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Host maintains a standing force of approximately twelve thousand soldiers, with additional reserves that can be mobilized during times of border conflict or internal unrest.",
      "since": "998"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Commanders of the Frostwing Host are appointed by Tsar Dmitry IV himself from among experienced veterans, with senior officers typically drawn from pure-line Snowy Owl-folk families of military tradition.",
      "since": "994"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Host's regimental structure includes the White Talon as its heavy infantry and the Frosted Wing as its elite scout archers, with additional specialized units organized according to terrain and mission.",
      "since": "994"
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Winter campaigns are the Frostwing's strongest season, as the long northern nights and frozen terrain align perfectly with Owl-folk capabilities, while enemy forces from warmer climates often struggle to conduct operations in such conditions.",
      "since": "994"
    }
  ],
