{ "name": "The Academy of the Chiseled Moon",
  "aka": [],
  "tag": "institution",
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The central administrative seat of the Talon-Scribe Order, housed in a great stone hall within the inner quarter of Velikoye, the Academy of the Chiseled Moon serves as the headquarters from which the Order oversees all rune-working across the Tsardom of Moscavia.",
      "since": null,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The building is constructed of pale granite quarried from the banks of the Khorol River, its walls rising four stories high and its roof pitched steeply to shed the heavy winter snows that bury Velikoye each year.",
      "since": null,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "Above the main entrance, carved into a lintel of dark basalt set into the granite facade, the Order's motto reads: 'By Talon and Stone, the Land Endures' — a phrase attributed to the first Chief Scribe appointed under Tsar Dmitry IV's Scribing Decree of 998.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The interior of the Academy is organized around a central courtyard open to the sky, where Novice scribes practice their chiseling on designated training stones set into the flagstone floor, their work visible to passing instructors through arched colonnades on every side.",
      "since": null,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "description",
      "text": "The eastern wing of the Academy contains a vast archive — a climate-controlled vault of iron-bound wooden cases — where copies of every rune pattern approved for public use across the Tsardom are stored on slabs of polished basalt, each inscription meticulously verified and updated by the Academy's clerical staff.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "history",
      "text": "The Academy was established in 972 as the Velikoye Rune Academy, a training institution for human practitioners of runic magic, predating the Blinding by twenty-two years.",
      "since": 972,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "history",
      "text": "After the Blinding of 994, the Academy remained closed for three years as the transition from human to Owl-folk stewardship was organized, its archives sealed and its training stones left untouched until the Order's formal reconstitution under the Scribing Decree.",
      "since": 994,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "history",
      "text": "Anastasiya Koroleva, the Academy's current Chief Scribe, survived the Blinding seated at her carving desk in the eastern wing, her half-finished mold still wet in its frame when the light struck — a detail that has become a touchstone of her reputation for unwavering dedication.",
      "since": 994,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "law",
      "text": "By the Scribing Decree of 998, the Academy is empowered to approve, modify, or reject any new rune design submitted for public use, a power exercised through the Chief Scribe and a council of senior registered scribes who convene monthly in the Academy's upper hall.",
      "since": 998,
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "The Academy also serves as the coordinating center for the Order's Corrupted Rune Site Investigation branch, from which teams of experienced scribes are dispatched across the Tsardom to assess and resolve dormant or corrupted rune sites left over from the era of human practitioners.",
      "held_by": null
    },
    {
      "category": "general",
      "text": "Within the Academy's walls, Chief Scribe Koroleva maintains a personal office in the northeastern corner of the second floor, identifiable by the deep gouges in the doorframe left by her talons — a habit she has never bothered to correct, and one that her staff has learned to regard as a mark of deep concentration rather than irritation.",
      "held_by": null
    }
  ],
